--TEST--
`Core\Cli\Progress::advance` has no spelling at all for a negative step, because `by` is a `uint` — `rule:tooling/in-place-output-is-a-scoped-live-region`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The low bound on a step is the *type's*, not the member's: a program that
// means to walk a bar backwards is refused a phase before any of its arithmetic
// runs, so there is nothing for the counting case beside this one to catch at
// run time. That is what makes a step of zero the smallest step there is, and
// why the two ends of `advance` are asked in two files.
Core\Cli::progress(2, fn(Core\Cli\Progress $bar): int => {
    $bar->advance({by: -1});
    return 0;
});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `uint`, found `int`
  --> case.nvs:%d:%d
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
